{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_ZIVz2PyIrZQ1RtpPgqDLsqxB","content":"345\t| yang.clojure: slice-6 case-arm fixtures are by constant KIND, not per corpus site — the plan's acceptance line asked for a minimal dispatch fixture for every arm of all six case sites (norm/proof keywords, mk-fresh numbers 0-3, typing symbols λ/Π); kinds are covered and mk-fresh runs end to end; closing route: derive fixtures from the corpus by walking the six sites, extracting each clause's constants, running a synthetic dispatch per arm+default (test-only addition) | slice 6 review (glm session 39b94aba), architect sign-off fable 8c1f0b7e | yang.clojure | slice 7 (test-only) | P3 |\n346\t| yang.clojure: no cljs/cljd lane evidence exists for the slice-6 commits yet (JVM + kondo only at sign-off time); the outcome-adapter reader-conditional catch remains the one host-sensitive line on the branch | slice 6 review (glm session 39b94aba, fifth item); architect condition: lanes green at 7677c12b before merge | yang.clojure | slice-6 landing gate (this merge) | P3 |\n347\t| yang.clojure: library `reduced?` matches any map holding :yin.k/reduced true (untyped tagged map, documented compromise in the library notes); closing route: a typed carrier if the VM gains one | slice 7 review (glm), fix round | yang.clojure | open | P3 |\n348\t| yang.clojure: a `kind/*` or other qualified export in value position ignores its published arities (the adapter falls back to 0-4, so a bad count reaches the host); closing route: feed module profiles into the adapter counts alongside `:native` | slice 7 review (glm), fix round | yang.clojure | slice 8 | P3 |\n349\t| yang.clojure: library-internal closures report the compiler's own source positions (:line/:column of the quoted library forms) in anonymous-fn arity errors; closing route: strip :line/:column metadata when building `library` | slice 7 review (glm), fix round | yang.clojure | slice 8 | P3 |\n350\t| yang.clojure: `library-for` counts only `defn` as a program definition; a `def`/`defn-`/`defmacro` redefinition of a library name over-pulls the library definition (harmless, the program definition wins); closing route: share the compile-program defined-names scan | slice 7 review (glm), fix round | yang.clojure | slice 8 | P3 |\n351\t| yang.clojure: `apply` surface gaps against Clojure, e.g. `(apply :k [{:k 1}])` fails loudly where Clojure returns 1; closing route: lower a keyword or collection operator in apply to the static lookup | slice 7 review (glm), fix round | yang.clojure | open | P3 |\n352\t| yang.clojure: the slice-9 kernel differential gate is honestly blocked at **107/165 credited (39 direct + 68 named integrations), 58 unexercised admitted arities**, 100 agreements, 2 recorded deviations (`elab-after-qed`, `check-after-qed`), 2 blocked fixtures, 2 declared upstream failures; the earlier 145/165-and-20 accounting predated the common-call reconciliation and under-counted (38 named-integration trace paths no longer exist) | hardening-3 H3-0 (the architect's finding: the deviation classifier required a bare closure where the reconciled compiler publishes the admitted §8.10 descriptor) | yang.clojure | H3-0 repaired the bookkeeping (versioned slice9_declarations.edn drives a representation-aware classifier with declared-call, message and script revalidation; the writer carries declared dispositions; a writer round-trip test replays the checked-in evidence) — repair, not closure; H3-1..H3-5 close the 58 per the approved hardening-3 plan | P2 |\n353\t\n354\t\n355\t## Closure notes: test-strategy-feedback-contract (2026-10-29)\n356\t"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_xAWezvuMw3RInfoN1AGxOE8b","content":"1\t# Slice 9 kernel differential gate: execution evidence correction\n2\t\n3\tThe gate on the hardening line is **blocked**. The architect denied the prior\n4\t165/165 closure claim because membership in a static dependency closure did\n5\tnot prove execution of every arity. That claim is withdrawn. The gate retains\n6\tits final assertion `(= :pass (:gate-status evidence))`; missing execution\n7\tevidence must fail that assertion.\n8\t\n9\tThe 106-fixture corpus has **100 passing agreements, two recorded deviations\n10\t(`elab-after-qed`, `check-after-qed`), two blocked fixtures, and two recorded\n11\tupstream failures.** The four narrowly recorded exception dispositions remain\n12\tdeclared departures, not agreements. No upstream or `src/cljc/` source changes\n13\tare made by H3-0. Admission is unchanged: 155 bindings (146 admitted, 9\n14\texcluded) and 175 candidate function/arities (165 admitted, 10 excluded).\n15\t\n16\tRecorded executions establish **107/165** admitted arities: 39 directly\n17\tand 68 through named integrations. The other **58**, including `parse/1`,\n18\tremain uncredited. The declared departures are carried by the versioned\n19\t[`slice9_declarations.edn`](slice9_declarations.edn) (provenance `ea18c8e4^`),\n20\trevalidated on every refresh by the representation-aware classifier: the\n21\tguest `:meta` value may be a pre-adoption raw closure or the admitted §8.10\n22\tdescriptor; structurally invalid descriptors and any payload, message, script\n23\tor call mismatch refuse (descriptor authenticity itself is the compiler's\n24\tadmission witness upstream of the outcome). The corrected counts and remaining arities\n25\tare recorded in [`slice9_evidence.edn`](slice9_evidence.edn) and\n26\t[`slice9_unexercised.edn`](slice9_unexercised.edn). The residual consumers in\n27\t[`fixture_closure.edn`](fixture_closure.edn) retain their concrete expected\n28\toutcomes; they do not establish closure of the full inventory, and their\n29\tcount (20) predates the re-derivation — the live unexercised set is the\n30\t58-name list.\n31\t\n32\t## Consumer evidence\n33\t\n34\t- `mkenv` preserves a nonempty global environment and creates empty locals.\n35\t- `beta-red`, `delta-normalize`, and `delta-normalize-local` have explicit\n36\t  entry fixtures and missing-reference rejections. The local wrapper also\n37\t  exercises explicit local definitions and their precedence over an ambient\n38\t  namespace definition.\n39\t- `install-unfold-implicit!` installs into both isolated upstream atoms on A.\n40\t  B/C return an updated immutable context, used by both the delta wrapper and\n41\t  NBE. Both normalizers read the same installed extension. An installed\n42\t  refusing extension propagates its original error data.\n43\t- `install-opacity-function` starts from a refusing policy, explicitly installs\n44\t  the working policy, then enters the original proof dispatcher through\n45\t  opaque/transparent steps and qed. A duplicate opaque step rejects. A uses\n46\t  an isolated namespace and host-local Var policy; B/C thread immutable\n47\t  definition updates through the explicit context.\n48\t- `install-fundamental-unparsers!` starts from an empty registry, installs the\n49\t  fundamental product unparser, then unparses nested implications. Dependent\n50\t  products and atoms remain unchanged. Direct `prod-impl-unparser` fixtures\n51\t  also verify its `[term false]` refusal result.\n52\t- `exists-kw?`, `term?`, `pair?`, and `vectorn?` include false results.\n53\t  `bound-vars` distinguishes a bound occurrence from entirely free variables.\n54\t  These fixtures preserve upstream behavior, including its shallow term\n55\t  validator and the use of `vector` rather than `vector?` in utility predicates.\n56\t- `proper-type?` enters each arity separately. Unknown variables throw;\n57\t  a well-typed term whose inferred type is not a sort returns false.\n58\t- `show-deftype` checks definition, axiom, theorem, implicit, and unknown\n59\t  labels. It depends only on portable record-kind predicates and returns a\n60\t  string. Host pprint and stdout functions remain excluded.\n61\t- `safe-get` covers successful lookup, missing keys, stored false, and stored\n62\t  nil. The latter three all reject upstream. `vremove` removes every match,\n63\t  preserves a no-match vector, and propagates a predicate's domain exception.\n64\t\n65\t`mkenv`, `appify`, and `bound-vars` have no domain rejection in the pinned\n66\tsource; the fixtures preserve their constructor, empty-input, and empty-set\n67\tresults instead of manufacturing refusals. A refused product rewrite is\n68\tidentified by its explicit modification flag, not mistaken for an exception.\n69\t\n70\tThe pinned local delta wrapper has a narrower portability scope than its\n71\tdocstring suggests: `delta-step` drops `local?` when calling `delta-reduction`\n72\ton a reference. Consequently upstream can resolve a global or host namespace\n73\tdefinition on that path. The global-result fixture preserves this behavior;\n74\tthe namespace fixture supplies a local definition that shadows the ambient\n75\tone. The guest boundary still requires explicit definitions and has no host\n76\tnamespace lookup capability. This round does not repair upstream or claim\n77\tagreement for ambient-only resolution.\n78\t\n79\t## Acceptance counting\n80\t\n81\tEvery selected guest function body appends `[guest-function arity]` to an\n82\texplicit diagnostic stream at entry. Instrumentation covers all arities of\n83\tthe functions supplied to each fixture, including higher-order calls through\n84\tregistries and extension closures. Each C lane creates its own stream.\n85\tAfter the VM halts, the harness reads that stream through its own\n86\tcursor, preserving the fixture's original outcome and exception payload.\n87\tA/B remain uninstrumented. Raw ordered call records are retained under\n88\t`:c-walker :executed-calls` and `:c-semantic :executed-calls` for every completed\n89\tfixture. The original uninstrumented fixtures used 1,000,000 instructions per\n90\tlane. The instrumented fixtures have a 2,000,000 instruction bound because\n91\tbody-entry stream writes add guest instructions. Reading the completed\n92\tdiagnostic stream is harness work after halt. This is an instrumentation\n93\tbudget change, not a new performance acceptance claim.\n94\t\n95\tPassing direct fixtures contribute only their original function/argument\n96\tcount, and only with matching body-entry records in both C lanes. Passing\n97\tnamed integrations contribute only exact arities recorded in both C lanes.\n98\tStatic dependency membership contributes no credit. Full branch coverage is\n99\tnot required. Context adapter identities and explicit extra context arguments\n100\tare recorded in the evidence; each observed guest arity is checked against\n101\tthat mapping individually, never against all arities of its function.\n102\t\n103\tOnly `:pass` fixture rows contribute exercise evidence. Recorded upstream\n104\tfailures and deviations do not contribute. Any admitted arity without a\n105\tpassing direct or named integration execution path blocks the gate.\n106\t\n107\tThe accounting regression first failed against the old implementation: it\n108\tcredited the deliberately uncalled arity and accepted missing C-lane traces.\n109\tIt now requires both traces and leaves unused arities uncredited. A second\n110\tregression replaces the adapted `parse/1` body in memory with an unconditional\n111\terror, then runs `:parse-to-normalize-to-type`. A/B and both C lanes still\n112\tpass; both C traces record `parse/2` and no `parse/1`, and the counter leaves\n113\t`parse/1` uncredited. Every credited path is also checked against the recorded\n114\texecutions of its named fixture. See\n115\t[`slice9_arity_accounting_test.txt`](slice9_arity_accounting_test.txt).\n116\t\n117\t## Recorded portability boundaries\n118\t\n119\tThe two `:recorded-deviation` rows remain `:elab-after-qed` and\n120\t`:check-after-qed`. Upstream embeds `clojure.core/meta`, a host function, in\n121\texception data; C carries a guest closure. The original outcomes, comparison\n122\tflags, exact payload guards, and evidence pointers remain intact. Both rows\n123\tare listed in `:recorded-portability-boundaries` in the summary. Neither is\n124\treported as agreement.\n125\t\n126\t## Recorded upstream failures\n127\t\n128\t`:typing-ascription` still reaches the upstream declaration\n129\t`type-of-ascribe`, which has no definition. A raises its original unbound-fn\n130\texception; B/C retain the explicit branch-local refusal.\n131\t\n132\t`:compile-malformed` still passes scalar proof input `[42]`. A/B raise the\n133\toriginal native sequence exception; C retains its portable sequence refusal.\n134\t\n135\tThese two rows have the distinct disposition `:recorded-upstream-failure` and\n136\tare listed in `:recorded-upstream-failures`. Their original A/B/C records and\n137\tfalse agreement flags remain available. The disposition checks the exact\n138\tfixture ID, input call, exception class/message, B outcome, and both completed\n139\tC outcomes. Changed calls, IDs, or C payloads are tested to refuse the\n140\tdisposition. Any other execution failure remains a blocker. No upstream fix,\n141\taccepted-negative claim, or equality projection is introduced for these rows.\n142\t\n143\t## Verification\n144\t\n145\tAn independent audit re-derives the credited arities and fixture paths from\n146\tthe two raw C traces. Kondo reports zero errors and warnings. The full oracle\n147\truns 26 tests and 1,689 assertions with exactly one failure and no errors:\n148\tits retained `(= :pass (:gate-status evidence))` closure assertion. The\n149\tunexercised arities — **58** under the current accounting, including\n150\t`parse/1` — therefore continue to block acceptance. Verification results are\n151\trecorded in [`slice9_verification.edn`](slice9_verification.edn), with command\n152\toutputs beside it.\n153\t`yang.latte-oracle-test/write-kernel-gate-evidence!` explicitly regenerates\n154\tboth execution evidence and the remaining-arity inventory; normal tests do\n155\tnot write them. Evidence retains the pinned upstream revision, compiler\n156\tdigest, runtime, instruction budget, per-fixture outcomes, diagnostic traces,\n157\tdependency graph, admission inventory, credited paths, and all four recorded\n158\texception dispositions.\n159\t\n160\tThe append-only correction in [`known-gaps.md`](../../../docs/agents/known-gaps.md)\n161\trecords that host Clojure turns a thrown string into `ClassCastException`,\n162\tcaught by `catch Exception` but not `catch ExceptionInfo`. Portable `try` binds\n163\tthe error payload without equivalent runtime class handling; this guest/host\n164\tgap remains declared.\n165\t\n166\tExecution scope is both C evaluators on the JVM. This correction does not\n167\tclaim renewed architect sign-off or Node/Dart verification, and the blocked\n168\tgate does not authorize program closure or merge."}
{"role":"assistant","content":"## Verdict: REVISE\n\nMost requested repairs landed, but three binding defects remain:\n\n1. **Copied descriptors still pass classification.**  \n   `kernel-callable-descriptor?` remains purely structural (`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1937-1952`). A descriptor copied wholesale from a genuine execution therefore passes, contrary to the Redo requirement to reject copied descriptors. No copied-descriptor control appears in `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2093-2142`. Delegating authenticity to the compiler does not make this classifier reject a forged or copied outcome supplied to it. The positive control still demonstrates the problem: two independently constructed closures are accepted as entry and witness without validating their relationship.\n\n2. **Shape-only mutation still passes.**  \n   The classifier still normalizes both scripts with `vec` (`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1975-1976`). Changing a script from a vector to a list with identical contents therefore preserves classification when A and C receive the same shape change. The controls at `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2108-2114` are unchanged: `[:new-mismatch]` changes payload, while `'()` changes both payload and shape. Neither is the claimed shape-only control.\n\n3. **The verification narrative is stale again.**  \n   `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_gate.md:145-148` says **1,689 assertions**, but the revised run is **1,695 assertions**.\n\nAdditionally, the earlier fixed-scope concern remains: declared `:boundary`, `:upstream-value`, `:reason`, and upstream revision are emitted without checking their required values (`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1994-1998,2024-2039`). If the versioned file is intended to be authoritative for metadata, this should at least be explicit; the current implementation does not itself guarantee that all four historical dispositions retain their exact scope and provenance.\n\nThe declared-call pins, upstream declaration usage, outcomes-marker checks, per-execution incompleteness controls, writer test, and removal of the H3-0 closure claim are otherwise correctly revised."}
